// CLAIM: One event per element
// HOLDS: refused
// REFUSED-BECAUSE: an element takes ONE `on:` binding
// WHY: a handler is an expression with no end marker, so the first `on:` takes the rest of the head.
//      If this ever stops being refused it will be because the head gained a delimiter, and then the
//      page should teach two events rather than apologise for one.
:props: n: Int
:!props:

:input: on:input=Msg.Draft(value) on:keydown=Msg.Add
:!input:
